{p})\\,},\n\\qquad\ny_{H}:=-\\frac{x_{p}(x_{p}-d)}{y_{p}} .\\tag{16}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 4.  The circum‑circle \\((BEF)\\)\n\nWrite the general equation of a circle as  \n\n\\[\nx^{2}+y^{2}+ux+vy+w=0 .\\tag{17}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the three points  \n\n\\[\nB=(x_{0},-y_{0}),\\qquad E=(x_{E},y_{E}),\\qquad F=(x_{F},y_{F})\n\\]\n\ninto (17) yields a linear system for \\(u,v,w\\).  Solving gives  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&= -2x_{0}+ \\frac{2\\bigl(x_{E}y_{F}-x_{F}y_{E}\\bigr)}\n                     {x_{E}y_{F}-x_{F}y_{E}+x_{0}(y_{E}-y_{F})},\\\\[2mm]\nv&= -2y_{0}+ \\frac{2\\bigl(y_{E}x_{F}-y_{F}x_{E}\\bigr)}\n                     {x_{E}y_{F}-x_{F}y_{E}+x_{0}(y_{E}-y_{F})},\\\\[2mm]\nw&= x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}+u x_{0}+v y_{0}.\n\\end{aligned}\\tag{18}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(y_{E}=y_{0}+m(x_{E}-x_{0})\\) and \\(y_{F}=y_{0}+m(x_{F}-x_{0})\\),\nevery occurrence of \\(y_{0}\\) appears together with the factor\n\\(x_{E}y_{F}-x_{F}y_{E}+x_{0}(y_{E}-y_{F})\\); using the relation\n\\(y_{0}^{2}=r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}\\) (which follows from (3)) all square‑roots cancel,\nso \\(u,v,w\\) are **rational functions** of the parameters \\(d,r,R\\).\n\nThe centre and radius of \\((BEF)\\) are therefore  \n\n\\[\nO_{1}= \\Bigl(-\\frac{u}{2},-\\frac{v}{2}\\Bigr),\\qquad \n\\rho^{2}= \\Bigl(\\frac{u^{2}+v^{2}}{4}\\Bigr)-w .\\tag{19}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 5.  Verification of the tangency  \n\nFor a line \\(y-y_{H}=m(x-x_{p})\\) the (perpendicular) distance from a point\n\\((x_{0},y_{0})\\) equals  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}= \\frac{|\\,m x_{0}-y_{0}+y_{H}-m x_{p}\\,|}\n                         {\\sqrt{m^{2}+1}} .\\tag{20}\n\\]\n\nApplying (20) to the centre \\(O_{1}=(-u/2,-v/2)\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}\\bigl(O_{1},\\;{\\rm line}\\;(16)\\bigr)\n   =\\frac{\\bigl|\\,m\\bigl(-\\frac{u}{2}\\bigr)+\\frac{v}{2}\n                +y_{H}-m x_{p}\\bigr|}\n          {